# Patterns the push sidecar keeps out of its "agent WIP" commits. They apply to new
# files, the ones HEAD does not have: a new file whose name, or the name of a
# directory above it, matches a pattern stays out of the commit, also when the
# agent staged it, and a push-note line names it. Changes to files HEAD already
# has are always committed, whatever their name, so an edit to a tracked
# .env.example is kept. The patterns apply on top of the repository's own
# .gitignore, and a negation there (!.env) does not bring a matching file back.
# Commits the agent made itself are pushed as they are. A pattern matches in any
# letter case, so *.key also keeps SERVER.KEY out and *credentials* keeps
# Credentials.json out.
#
# Sources checked:
#   id_rsa*, id_ecdsa*, id_ed25519*  default private key names in ssh-keygen(1),
#                                    https://man.openbsd.org/ssh-keygen
#   .npmrc      can hold _authToken and _password,
#               https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/configuring-npm/npmrc
#   .pypirc     holds usernames and PyPI tokens in plain text,
#               https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/pypirc/
#   .git-credentials  plain-text file of git-credential-store,
#               https://git-scm.com/docs/git-credential-store
#   auth.json   the file this image's Codex entrypoint writes the Codex login to
#   .envrc      direnv loads it, and lists "load secrets for deployment" as a use,
#               https://direnv.net/
#   kubeconfig, *.kubeconfig, .kube
#               kubeconfig files hold cluster credentials (client keys, tokens,
#               passwords); kubectl reads $HOME/.kube/config by default,
#               https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/organize-cluster-access-kubeconfig/
#   *.tfvars, *.tfvars.json
#               Terraform variable files; Terraform says to keep files with
#               sensitive values out of version control,
#               https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/values/variables
#   *.tfstate, *.tfstate.*
#               Terraform state, a plaintext file that includes secret values
#               (https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/state/sensitive-data);
#               terraform.tfstate is the local backend's default name and backups
#               take it as a prefix,
#               https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/backend/local
# Not verified against a published document, kept as common practice: .env, .env.*,
# *.pem, *.key, *.p12, *.pfx, *credentials*, .netrc.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*credentials*
.npmrc
.pypirc
.netrc
.git-credentials
auth.json
.envrc
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
.kube
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
